conductor-idp-selinux: SELinux policy for conductor-idp
=======================================================

The module "conductor_idp" (targeted policy, priority 200) confines
/usr/bin/conductor-idp (conductor-idp.service, user conductor-idp) in
conductor_idp_t.

File types:

  conductor_idp_conf_t     /etc/conductor-idp (idp.toml, domain CA, tls/)
  conductor_idp_cred_t     /etc/conductor-idp/credentials (read by systemd only)
  conductor_idp_var_lib_t  /var/lib/conductor-idp (clients, keys, audit log)

conductor-idp listens on its HTTPS port (9443 by default, which the base
policy types pki_ca_port_t, like 9444 to 9447 for a separate admin
listener; http_port_t ports are allowed too) and connects to the domain
controllers over LDAP/LDAPS and Kerberos. A port with no type yet:

  semanage port -a -t http_port_t -p tcp 9480

Troubleshooting:

  ausearch -m AVC,USER_AVC -ts recent -c conductor-idp
  semanage permissive -a conductor_idp_t     (and -d to revert)

License
-------

The policy sources here (.te, .fc, .if, .cil) are Apache-2.0, like the
rest of the repository. The compiled modules expand macros and interfaces
of the SELinux reference policy shipped by selinux-policy-devel, which is
GPL-2.0-or-later, so the binary package is licensed "Apache-2.0 AND
GPL-2.0-or-later" and carries the reference policy's COPYING in
/usr/share/licenses/<package>/THIRD-PARTY-LICENSES. Apache-2.0 alone is
not possible for the compiled modules. The corresponding source is this
repository at the release commit and the Fedora selinux-policy source
package of the version the modules were compiled against.
